# A streamed turn must not overwrite a child ask's probed questions.
#
# A parent cannot see which of a child's keys really take a file, so
# elicitation.h coerces every non-`_other` prose key of a child ask to File.
# The polled path undoes that with a probe of the child; the streamed path
# (loader_system's adopt_turn_asks) re-derives the asks straight from the
# turn's own state and had no probe to undo it with. The typed answer then had
# nowhere to live -- content_object skips File questions, so a submit went out
# without it -- while the card blamed the file question it had just invented.
#
# HANABI_ASK_DEMO=child gives t2 a child ask whose questions are already
# resolved (what a probe produces: a picker and one prose key, no file key at
# all) and makes the mock's streaming turn report that same ask in the parent's
# coerced shape. Send a message and the prose key must still be a prose key.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_ASK_DEMO=child

require_thread t2
expect_text "The sub-agent cannot book the correction without a cycle."
expect_no_text "answer it in the sub-agent's thread"

click_ui ask_text_q3
wait_frames 4
type "the payout owner already signed it"
wait_frames 4
expect_input_text ask_text_q3 "the payout owner already signed it"

click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4
type "carry on"
wait_frames 4
key ENTER
wait_frames 60

# The turn really landed -- this is the mock's own reply, not the draft.
expect_text "I'll follow up here as I make progress."
# ...and q3 is still a field the user can answer, holding what they typed.
expect_no_text "answer it in the sub-agent's thread"
expect_input_text ask_text_q3 "the payout owner already signed it"
